<div class="admin-oauth-clients" data-page="oauth-request-refused" data-error="fetch_metadata">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Request refused</h1>
  <p class="alert alert-error my-4 max-w-3xl" role="alert">
    This action must be submitted with its button in the same browser window. Your browser did not send the information
    that proves it, so nothing was changed.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70 mb-4 max-w-3xl">
    If you used a script or an embedded page, open the page and press the button yourself.
    Use a current Chrome, Firefox or Safari: an old browser, or a proxy that removes the Sec-Fetch headers, cannot be used for this action.
    <span :if={String.starts_with?(@back_path, "/admin/oauth")}>
      The operator command line can revoke a client without a browser (see the deployment guide).
    </span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href={@back_path} class="link link-primary" data-role="back-to-list">{back_label(@back_path)}</a>
  </p>
</div>
